{"repositoryId":2511505,"availability":"available","full":"jsonform/jsonform","name":"jsonform","description":"Build forms from JSON Schema. Easily template-able. Compatible with Bootstrap 3 out of the box.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":2817,"forks":545,"created":"2011-10-04T12:05:48Z","updated":"2024-06-19T15:28:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://jsonform.github.io/jsonform/playground/index.html","topics":["forms","html5","javascript","json","json-form","json-schema"],"demo":"https://jsonform.github.io/jsonform/playground/index.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:20.759Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:20.759Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:20.759Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.662Z","stars":2818,"forks":545},{"at":"2026-10-19T15:55:20.759Z","stars":2817,"forks":545}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The JSON Form library is a JavaScript client-side library that takes a structured data model defined using JSON Schema as input and returns a Bootstrap 3-friendly HTML form that matches the schema.","The generated HTML form includes client-side validation logic that provides direct inline feedback to the user upon form submission (provided a JSON Schema validator is available). If values are valid, the JSON Form library uses submitted values to create the JavaScript data structure that matches the data model.","The layout of the generated HTML form may be entirely fine-tuned through a simple declarative mechanism."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jsonform/jsonform/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"dbe5131e219d8e18e673706859755edc64252622320f44ac69b626e6fe802e6c","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.763Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.763Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The JSON Form library is a JavaScript client-side library that takes a structured data model defined using JSON